 "Same three tokens, very different meaning. The embedding table E alone gives the same three vectors in both sentences; only their <0>order</0> differs.": "",
 "▼ Dive in: <0>Demo</0>": "",
 "Attention treats its input as a <0>set</0>: shuffle the tokens and each token's output is the same, just moved. Without extra information, \"dog bites man\" = \"man bites dog\".": "",
 "So the model must be told <0>where</0> each token is: by adding position vectors, or by rotating Q and K (RoPE).": "",
 "Demo uses plain self-attention without a causal mask. With a causal mask a model can infer a little order implicitly, but it is weak and unreliable.": "",
 "Modern LLMs such as the 8B reference use RoPE (next slide).": "",
