 "▼ Dive in: <0>Relative offset</0>": "",
 "RoPE rotates each (even, odd) pair of numbers in Q and K by an angle <0>proportional to the token's position</0>.": "",
 "Because rotations compose, the dot product q·k then depends only on the <0>relative offset</0> between the two tokens.": "",
 "Different pairs rotate at different speeds θᵢ = base^(−2i/d_head): fast pairs resolve nearby offsets, slow pairs long distances.": "",
 "RoPE is applied to Q and K inside each attention layer, not added to the embedding. The toy matrix X later is a simplification.": "",
